# Known upstream GLib leak (observed on glib 2.88.3): when GSocketClient runs an
# internal multi-address connection attempt ("happy eyeballs", e.g. connecting to
# "localhost" which resolves to [::1, 127.0.0.1]) and the first attempt is refused,
# a 16-byte allocation belonging to the discarded attempt is never freed.
#
# Reproducer: the plain-GLib baseline ("/.../stress/native") benchmark. An
# equivalent test using single-address connects (as "/.../stress/ours" does) or
# resolver-only lookups does NOT leak, which shows the allocation is owned by
# GSocketClient's retry machinery and not by gplusplus code.
leak:libgio-2.0.so.0